  "about": "Majority wins against expected rank and the posterior mean, on the postrank theory book's ch. 10 law on orders, the simulated league and KRW's 97 firms. The law on orders carries v1's ten expectations of the Deeper box of which-ranking (orders-er-* from the base-R oracles expectedRank-tb10-law051 and rankSummaries-tb10-law051; orders-wins-*, orders-pi-ab, orders-pi-bc, orders-p-abc and orders-p-cba from v1's frozen registry, tb10.law051.*), plus the two that v1 showed without an expectation (orders-p-bca, orders-pi-ac). League numbers are rows of the base-R oracle (normalPosterior at prior SD .15 and .05) or registry keys (exact expected ranks; the count of pairs the posterior-mean and expected-rank orders put differently, which is the expected-rank order's count against the majority because majority wins give the posterior-mean order on the league). KRW numbers are rows of the base-R oracle of the v3 helpers (majorityWins-krw-race and -gender: win counts and the cycle count), the postrank 1.1.0 golden row of KRW's lambda = 1 race card evaluated on the released race array (N, G, M), or registry keys (the posterior-mean order's stated pairs above one half, its expected wrong claims, the card's DR). Not covered by expectations (data-num only): the expected-rank order's count against the majority on KRW's gaps (62 race, 171 gender), the gender card's counts, the cycle's pair probabilities, the bars' probabilities and the formula's terms other than its results.",
